---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Verify You're Using Cutline">
  <h1>Verify You're Using Cutline</h1>

  <section class="intro">
    <p class="lead">
      After configuring your DNS, follow these steps to confirm you're using the cut path.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="dns-check">
    <h2>Automatic DNS Check</h2>
    <p>Click the button below to check if this device is using Cutline DNS:</p>
    
    <button id="check-button" class="check-button">Check Now</button>
    
    <div id="status-banner" class="status-banner status-idle">
      <strong>Not checked yet.</strong> Click "Check Now" to test.
    </div>

    <details class="how-it-works">
      <summary>How this check works</summary>
      <div class="details-content">
        <p>
          When you click "Check Now," your browser silently probes two hostnames:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><code>on.thecutline.org</code> — exists <strong>only</strong> on Cutline DNS, not in public DNS</li>
          <li><code>off.thecutline.org</code> — exists in public DNS but is on the Cutline block overlay, so a cut path must return NXDOMAIN</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          <strong>Green (you are on a cut path) only if:</strong> the first fetch succeeds <strong>and</strong> the second fetch fails.
        </p>
        <p>
          Any other combination means you are not on a cut path. If both succeed, you are either using public DNS, 
          a mixed resolver, or Cutline is not blocking the off probe (leak). If the on probe fails, you are not 
          using Cutline DNS. If both fail, you are not on a cut path.
        </p>
        <p>
          You are not sent to either hostname. The check is performed silently in JavaScript with fetch, 
          and all errors are caught by this page.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>
  </section>

  <section class="steps">
    <h2>Test Steps</h2>

    <div class="test-step">
      <div class="step-number">1</div>
      <div class="step-content">
        <h3>Quit and Restart Safari (macOS/iOS)</h3>
        <p>
          Safari caches DNS aggressively. On macOS, fully quit Safari (⌘Q), then reopen it. 
          On iOS, swipe up to close Safari completely, then reopen.
        </p>
        <p>
          Other browsers may also cache DNS. If testing in Chrome or Firefox, restart them as well.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="test-step">
      <div class="step-number">2</div>
      <div class="step-content">
        <h3>Test Normal Sites Work</h3>
        <p>
          Visit a normal website to confirm DNS is working:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="https://example.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">example.com</a> — Should load</li>
          <li><a href="https://wikipedia.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">wikipedia.org</a> — Should load</li>
          <li><a href="https://github.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">github.com</a> — Should load</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          If these sites don't load, your DNS configuration may be incorrect. Double-check the settings.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="test-step">
      <div class="step-number">3</div>
      <div class="step-content">
        <h3>Run the Automatic Check</h3>
        <p>
          Use the <strong>Automatic DNS Check</strong> button at the top of this page to verify 
          you're on the cut path. This is the easiest and most reliable verification method.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="test-step">
      <div class="step-number">4</div>
      <div class="step-content">
        <h3>Use the Canary (Connection Proof, Not DNS Proof)</h3>
        <p>
          Visit the HTTP canary by IP address to confirm you can reach the resolver infrastructure:
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href="http://64.176.200.99/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="canary-link">http://64.176.200.99/</a>
        </p>
        <p class="canary-note">
          <strong>Important:</strong> This canary proves you can connect to this path, <strong>NOT</strong> 
          that you're using these DNS servers. It is connectivity verification only.
        </p>
        <p>
          The hostname canary <code>on.narge.test</code> exists but is weak in Safari (may be bypassed by search).
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="dns-check-tools">
    <h2>Command-Line DNS Check (Advanced)</h2>
    <p>
      If you're comfortable with terminal/command prompt, you can directly query Cutline DNS:
    </p>
    
    <h3>macOS/Linux</h3>
    <pre><code>dig @64.176.200.99 example.com</code></pre>
    <p>Should return an address for example.com.</p>

    <h3>Windows</h3>
    <pre><code>nslookup example.com 64.176.200.99</code></pre>
    <p>Should return an address for example.com.</p>

    <h3>Test a Blocked Domain</h3>
    <p>
      Query a domain from the StevenBlack list. It should return <code>NXDOMAIN</code> (no such domain).
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="troubleshooting">
    <h2>Troubleshooting</h2>

    <h3>Normal sites don't load</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Double-check the DNS server IPs: <code>64.176.200.99</code> and <code>149.28.79.49</code></li>
      <li>Restart your device or renew DHCP</li>
      <li>Try flushing DNS cache (see below)</li>
      <li>On Windows, make sure you selected "Manual" DNS, not "Automatic"</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Blocked sites still load</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Fully quit and restart your browser (especially Safari)</li>
      <li>Check that your device isn't using another DNS source (VPN, proxy, corporate network)</li>
      <li>On iOS, verify DNS is set for the specific Wi-Fi network you're on</li>
      <li>The site may not be in the block list (the list is an approximation)</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Flush DNS Cache</h3>
    <p><strong>macOS:</strong></p>
    <pre><code>sudo dscacheutil -flushcache; sudo killall -HUP mDNSResponder</code></pre>

    <p><strong>Windows:</strong></p>
    <pre><code>ipconfig /flushdns</code></pre>

    <p><strong>Linux:</strong></p>
    <pre><code>sudo systemd-resolve --flush-caches</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section class="help">
    <h2>Still Having Issues?</h2>
    <p>
      If you're stuck, check the <a href="/docs">docs</a> or open an issue on 
      <a href="https://github.com/dov-max/narge-spec/issues" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>

<script>
  function checkDNS() {
    const banner = document.getElementById('status-banner');
    const button = document.getElementById('check-button');
    
    if (!banner || !button) return;
    
    // Set checking state
    banner.className = 'status-banner status-checking';
    banner.innerHTML = '<strong>Checking...</strong>';
    button.disabled = true;
    
    // Probe both endpoints
    const onProbe = fetch('https://on.thecutline.org/ok', {
      method: 'GET',
      cache: 'no-store',
      mode: 'cors'
    });
    
    const offProbe = fetch('https://off.thecutline.org/ok', {
      method: 'GET',
      cache: 'no-store',
      mode: 'cors'
    });
    
    // Wait for both probes to complete (or fail)
    Promise.allSettled([onProbe, offProbe])
      .then(results => {
        const onResult = results[0];
        const offResult = results[1];
        
        // Check if on succeeded (200)
        const onSuccess = onResult.status === 'fulfilled' && onResult.value.ok;
        
        // Check if off failed (network/DNS error)
        const offFailed = offResult.status === 'rejected';
        
        // Green ONLY if on succeeds AND off fails
        if (onSuccess && offFailed) {
          banner.className = 'status-banner status-success';
          banner.innerHTML = `
            <strong>You are on a cut path.</strong>
            <p class="status-note">Another DNS, a VPN, or Private Relay can skip Cutline.</p>
          `;
        } else {
          // Any other combination: not on cut path
          showNotOnCutPath(banner);
        }
        
        button.disabled = false;
      });
  }
  
  function showNotOnCutPath(banner) {
    banner.className = 'status-banner status-fail';
    banner.innerHTML = `
      <strong>You are not on a cut path.</strong>
      <p class="status-note">Another DNS, a VPN, or Private Relay can skip Cutline.</p>
    `;
  }
  
  // Auto-run check on page load
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    checkDNS();
  });
  
  // Button click handler
  const checkButton = document.getElementById('check-button');
  if (checkButton) {
    checkButton.addEventListener('click', checkDNS);
  }
</script>

<style>
  .intro {
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xl);
  }

  .lead {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .dns-check {
    margin: var(--spacing-2xl) 0;
    padding: var(--spacing-xl);
    background: var(--color-card-bg);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    border: 2px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .dns-check h2 {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .check-button {
    background: var(--color-accent);
    color: white;
    border: none;
    padding: var(--spacing-md) var(--spacing-xl);
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    cursor: pointer;
    margin: var(--spacing-md) 0;
    transition: background 0.2s;
  }

  .check-button:hover:not(:disabled) {
    background: var(--color-accent-hover);
  }

  .check-button:disabled {
    opacity: 0.6;
    cursor: not-allowed;
  }

  .status-banner {
    padding: var(--spacing-lg);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    margin: var(--spacing-lg) 0;
    border-left: 4px solid #ccc;
  }

  .status-banner strong {
    display: block;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xs);
  }

  .status-note {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin: var(--spacing-xs) 0 0 0;
  }

  .status-idle {
    background: #f5f5f5;
    border-left-color: #999;
  }

  .status-checking {
    background: #e3f2fd;
    border-left-color: #2196f3;
  }

  .status-success {
    background: #e8f5e9;
    border-left-color: #4caf50;
  }

  .status-fail {
    background: #fff3e0;
    border-left-color: #ff9800;
  }

  .how-it-works {
    margin-top: var(--spacing-xl);
    padding: var(--spacing-md);
    background: #fafafa;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .how-it-works summary {
    cursor: pointer;
    font-weight: 600;
    padding: var(--spacing-sm);
    user-select: none;
  }

  .how-it-works summary:hover {
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }

  .details-content {
    padding: var(--spacing-md) var(--spacing-sm) 0;
  }

  .details-content p {
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-md);
  }

  .steps {
    margin: var(--spacing-2xl) 0;
  }

  .test-step {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--spacing-lg);
    margin: var(--spacing-xl) 0;
    padding: var(--spacing-lg);
    background: var(--color-card-bg);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
  }

  .step-number {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: 3rem;
    height: 3rem;
    background: var(--color-accent);
    color: white;
    border-radius: 50%;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .step-content {
    flex: 1;
  }

  .step-content h3 {
    margin-top: 0;
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
  }

  .step-content ul {
    padding-left: var(--spacing-lg);
  }

  .step-content li {
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xs);
  }

  .warning {
    background: #fff3cd;
    border-left: 4px solid #ffc107;
    padding: var(--spacing-md);
    margin: var(--spacing-md) 0;
    border-radius: 4px;
    color: #856404;
  }

  .canary-link {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    padding: var(--spacing-sm) var(--spacing-md);
    background: var(--color-card-bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 4px;
    margin: var(--spacing-sm) 0;
  }

  .canary-note {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-style: italic;
  }

  .dns-check-tools,
  .troubleshooting,
  .help {
    margin: var(--spacing-2xl) 0;
  }

  h3 {
    margin-top: var(--spacing-xl);
    font-size: 1.25rem;
  }

  pre {
    background: var(--color-text);
    color: #f8f8f2;
    padding: var(--spacing-md);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    overflow-x: auto;
  }

  pre code {
    color: #f8f8f2;
  }

  ul {
    padding-left: var(--spacing-lg);
  }

  li {
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .test-step {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: var(--spacing-sm);
    }

    .step-number {
      width: 2.5rem;
      height: 2.5rem;
      font-size: 1.25rem;
    }
  }
</style>
